Like I said, didn't bring a lot of stuff.

About the game itself, it was pretty interesting.  I found 2 WoW on
dlevel 2 and got most of an AK, so the early game was pretty easy,
Soko ->Mines.  I spent a great deal of time in Minetown, chillin with
a succubus and saccing, but all I ever got was Giantslayer, crowning,
and a whole lotta luck.  Medusa was the titan version, no worries.
Fort Ludios was fun, got a ton of gold and food.  Quest was a great
source of strength... for someone without gauntlets of power at
least.  Castle was easy, the fabled drawbridge was no challenge.  I
played mastermind, then retreated to the corridors to pick off each
enemy till warning told me there was nothing left in the courtyard and
I crossed the bridge.  Had a scary moment where my BoH got cursed, but
I cancelled it and all was well.  Another scary moment earlier when I
drank from a sink and got polymorphed.  Lost shirt and robe, had to
get more with polypiling and wishing.  Before Genhennom I blessed and
enchanted all my stuff, which used most of my magic marker charges.  I
actually only had 5 magic mapping scrolls :( and two of them were used
on lairs :(((.  Found Vlad and ID'd the bad amulet.  Vlad was a joke.
Found the VS, marked with burned E, dropped the candelabrum, and
ported back up to the mines to get the bell and make final ascension
run arrangements.  Ported back down... to Mine's End.  Oops.  Back out
the main dungeon and ported down... to the Valley.  Oops again.  I
finally got to the VS level and set out to get Rodney.  On the way up
I got some wraith corpses.  I had started Gehennom at XL24, ended at
XL28.  I had to wish up scrolls of gold detection as I'd never seen
them and two attempts at writing failed.  Oh well.  I foolishly tried
to fight Rodney and got most of my stuff moved to uncursed for my
troubles before a death ray killed him.  Then the mad dash to the VS,
then the Sanctum, which was easy with conflict.  Everything just
killed itself and let me by.  Killed the priest, got the Amulet, and
off to the races.  Mysterious force was pretty bad, had to do
Baalzebub's lair three times, which is a pain as it's no teleport,
undiggable, and the stairs were far apart.  Rodney appeared in the
Valley twice and once in the main dungeon, but never got away with the
Amulet.  He did quaff a gain level potion, though.  Dunno what that
would do for him.  Dash out of the dungeon and off to Earth.  Earth
was pretty bad, actually.  I had to use 2 scrolls to find the portal
and got the Amulet cursed onto me trying to find it, and had to pray
it off.  (I had lost my holy water when I dropped it forgetting I was
levitating).  Anyway, the other planes were easy, especially with
conflict.  Astral was scary, but the altar was the first I picked,
Famine's.  Death ray to the face, then a sprint to the door.  Chatted
for two bits for ale, because I gotta be a CLASSY demigod.  Then
ascension.
Obviously the WoWs really handed me the game, and I basically just
never messed up badly enough to counter that advantage.  I was
essentially invulnerable to most enemies and never had low health or
resistance issues.  It was a pretty cool game, and I liked it,
considering I'd never even seen Sokoban before.  The oddest thing was
the time gap.  I started this game and finished up to Medusa last
winter, and just did the rest in the past week or so.  I did
everything post-Castle today, in fact.  Maybe next I'll do lawful, cuz
I wanna try Grayswandir.  I'm also sort of interested in SLASH 'EM,
with cool monks and guns and suchlike.  Anyway, peace.




